branch: feature/fact-declaring
worktree: ../okay-wt-decl
spec: docs/di.md, specs/di.md (module-facts / di-facts-examples)

why: two things the operator found by reading the example. (1) A
  contribution could not read the capability its OWN module installs,
  so one feature had to be split into a capability module and a
  contribution module — proved liftable: compute the fact inside the
  module's own installer. (2) `contributing(k, v)` takes both
  arguments in one list, so the block needs a `: Routes` ascription;
  curried, the second list is typed by `Fact[V]` and the ascription
  goes.

what: `declare(k)(v)`, `contributing(k)(v)` curried; new
  `declaring(k)(v: F[V])` for a fact that reads what its module
  installs. Call sites updated (TestModule, Needs.needs,
  TestRouteFacts), and the routes example rewritten to the shape a
  reader expects: one feature, one module, its capability and its
  routes together.

next: core, call sites, example, docs
